  "verbalization": "Bisdehydrostemonine appears to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular targets, with A172 and Free fatty acid receptor 2 acting as intermediate nodes in the pathway. The final scores from the three paths suggest a consistent but not absolute relationship, with the highest confidence in the interaction through Free fatty acid receptor 2 and 1-Epitatridin B. The mechanism involves a cascade of targets, where Bisdehydrostemonine may modulate signaling pathways that ultimately influence Phosphodiesterase 6C activity. The presence of multiple independent pathways supports the hypothesis, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a plausible biological link, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct effect of Bisdehydrostemonine on Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
